description: Robust pattern for ambiguous queries in React Testing Library
globs: packages/frontend/src/components/**/*.test.tsx
alwaysApply: true
---

- **Always scope queries with `within` or use `data-testid` for elements that appear in multiple places**
  - When the same text appears in both a list and a detail view, use `within(container).getByText(...)` to avoid ambiguity
  - Add `data-testid` to containers (e.g., detail panels) for robust selection
  - Example:
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Scope to the session list
  const sessionList = screen.getByRole('listbox', { name: 'Session List' });
  expect(within(sessionList).getByText('Morning Session')).toBeInTheDocument();

  // ✅ DO: Scope to the detail view
  const detailView = screen.getByTestId('session-detail');
  expect(within(detailView).getByText('Morning Session')).toBeInTheDocument();

  // ❌ DON'T: Use screen.getByText('Morning Session') when the text appears in multiple places
  ```
  - Reference: See AgendaPanel tests for implementation.